The whole Playwright suite was run as well, because `send`'s retyping, the reducer branch and
the 差异 panel markup are shared by every other case in it:

    Running 81 tests using 1 worker
      6 skipped
      75 passed (1.5m)

Those six are the viewport-conditional cases in `e2e/phone-shell.pw.ts`, each of which skips
on whichever project it does not apply to: `the drawer only exists at phone width` on desktop,
`the docked sidebar only exists at desktop width` on mobile. They are conditional skips on
`main` too, and none of them reads the diff state.

The third case is the one worth reading in full, because it is the behaviour rather than the
plumbing: a file is written through the browser, then changed on disk by the test process,
then 回滚变更 is clicked. The alert says `note.txt 在写入之后又被改过，回滚会覆盖那次修改`,
the file on disk keeps the outside edit, the preview stays open, and after the test puts the
original bytes back the same proposal rolls back successfully. A refusal that also destroyed
the preview, or that consumed the proposal, would have failed that case.

== 6. What is still not covered

- Undo points live in the process. Restarting the host forgets every proposal, and the
  browser shows nothing for a write it did not see in this session. Persisting them is a
  separate design question: the recorded old side can be large, and a stale proposal surviving
  a restart would be a proposal to overwrite edits made while nothing was watching.
- A rollback does not emit `touched_path`, so an editor buffer holding the file keeps its own
  text until it is re-opened. Emitting it needs a `DiffAdapter` trait change, and the file
  list re-reads from disk on navigation, so the visible cost today is limited to an open
  buffer.
- Partial hunks remain unimplemented everywhere. One write is one proposal, accepted or
  rolled back whole; the `xai-grok-pager-diff` and `xai-hunk-tracker` integrations `TODO.md`
  asks for are still absent, and nothing in this batch pretends otherwise.
- Binary content is refused, not shown. The refusal is tested; a real binary diff is not.
- Only the 差异 panel's own controls are driven in a browser. The older 待审查差异提案 banner
  in the chat tab shares `acceptDiff` and `rollbackDiff`, so it benefits from the `session_id`
  fix, but no case clicks it there.

Reproduce the tests with the four commands in section 3; the mutations are single-line edits
to `crates/codegen/chaos-engine/src/lib.rs`, `crates/codegen/xai-grok-web/src/main.rs`,
`apps/chaos-ui/src/session.ts` and `apps/chaos-ui/src/main.tsx`, each named by the text it
replaces in section 4.
